  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Dry today, but daily rainfall chances arrive\nagain beginning on Saturday.\n\nHigh pressure will remain in control through today, but will\nbegin to weaken and shift east into the Atlantic by Saturday.\nShould still expect mostly clear skies through tonight, with\nhigh temperatures returning to normal for end of July. As\nsurface high pressure shifts east, will see return flow \nintroduce increasing moisture back into the region. An \napproaching upper level low, slowly moving east, will also bring\na return to daily rainfall chances beginning on Saturday. This \nwave will elongate and make very little progress through next \nweek. This will keep daily rain and thunderstorm chances through\nthe middle of next week. \n\nOverall, pattern is not supportive of organized severe, but \nrepetitive slow moving daily thunderstorms may begin to \nincrease hydro concerns through the middle of next week. \nPrecipitable Water values (approaching 2 inches) gives some \nconfidence in this as well. Temperatures next week generally at \nor slightly below normal.",
